{number: 61}
{title: O That Will Be Glory}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] When all my labors and trials are o'er,
And I am safe on that beautiful [G7] shore,
[C] Just to be near the dear Lord I adore,
Will thro' the [G7] ages be glory for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O that will be [F] glory for [C] me,
Glory for [G7] me, glory for [C] me,
When by His [C7] grace I shall [F] look on His [Dm] face,
That will be [C] glory, be [G7] glory for [C] me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] When by the gift of His infinite grace,
I am accorded in heaven a [G7] place,
[C] Just to be there and to look on His face,
Will thro' the [G7] ages be glory for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Friends will be there I have loved long ago;
Joy like a river around me will [G7] flow;
[C] Yet just a smile from my Savior, I know,
Will thro' the [G7] ages be glory for [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
